      "note_id": "old_shared_words",
      "kind": "helpful_transfer",
      "text": "English and Macedonian are distant cousins: both come from the same ancient ancestor, so look-alike words are few, and thousands of years have changed how the shared ones sound. Most of the words here (brother, sister, mother, two, three, ten, night, new, water, name, nose, salt, wolf, goose, beard) are old shared words: true relatives, not borrowings. The last two, vampire and robot, are words of Slavic origin that English borrowed, so they look alike: robot came into both languages from Czech.",
      "pairs": [
        {"from": "brother", "to": "брат", "to_ipa": "brat"},
        {"from": "sister", "to": "сестра", "to_ipa": "ˈsɛstra"},
        {"from": "mother", "to": "мајка", "to_ipa": "ˈmajka"},
        {"from": "two", "to": "два", "to_ipa": "dva"},
        {"from": "three", "to": "три", "to_ipa": "tri"},
        {"from": "ten", "to": "десет", "to_ipa": "ˈdɛsɛt"},
        {"from": "night", "to": "ноќ", "to_ipa": "nɔc"},
        {"from": "new", "to": "нов", "to_ipa": "nɔf"},
        {"from": "water", "to": "вода", "to_ipa": "ˈvɔda"},
        {"from": "name", "to": "име", "to_ipa": "ˈimɛ"},
        {"from": "nose", "to": "нос", "to_ipa": "nɔs"},
        {"from": "salt", "to": "сол", "to_ipa": "sɔɫ"},
        {"from": "wolf", "to": "волк", "to_ipa": "vɔɫk"},
        {"from": "goose", "to": "гуска", "to_ipa": "ˈɡuska"},
        {"from": "beard", "to": "брада", "to_ipa": "ˈbrada", "to_meaning": "beard (it can also mean chin)"},
        {"from": "vampire", "to": "вампир", "to_ipa": "ˈvampir"},
        {"from": "robot", "to": "робот", "to_ipa": "ˈrɔbɔt"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "note_id": "false_friends",
      "kind": "false_friend",
      "text": "A few look-alikes mean something different, some of them only when you sound the Cyrillic out. These are the ones that catch people out.",
      "pairs": [
        {"from": "magazine", "to": "магазин", "to_ipa": "maɡaˈzin", "to_meaning": "a warehouse, a storeroom"},
